{"id": "EUVD-2026-80464", "enisaUuid": "36d778c7-5eae-398f-b0c0-b50990388ef9", "description": "In the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\nscsi: qla2xxx: Bound i2c->length in I2C bsg handlers\n\nstruct qla_i2c_access carries a 16-bit length field alongside a fixed\n64-byte buffer:\n\n\tstruct qla_i2c_access {\n\t\tuint16_t device, offset, option, length;\n\t\tuint8_t  buffer[0x40];\n\t} __packed;\n\nqla2x00_write_i2c() and qla2x00_read_i2c() use the user-supplied\ni2c->length without any bounds check. i2c is overlaid on a 256-byte\non-stack buffer and sfp is a 256-byte DMA-pool buffer, so a length up to\n65535 overruns both:\n\n  - write: memcpy(sfp, i2c->buffer, i2c->length) over-reads the stack and\n    over-writes the sfp heap buffer, and qla2x00_write_sfp() then DMAs\n    i2c->length bytes out of the 256-byte buffer.\n  - read: qla2x00_read_sfp() DMAs i2c->length bytes into the 256-byte sfp,\n    then memcpy(i2c->buffer, sfp, i2c->length) overflows the 64-byte\n    buffer inside the on-stack array.\n\nA caller holding CAP_SYS_RAWIO can use this to corrupt the heap and the\nkernel stack. Reject requests whose length exceeds the buffer before any\ncopy or DMA transfer in both handlers.", "datePublished": "2026-09-16T10:31:35", "dateUpdated": "2026-10-19T08:53:57", "baseScore": 0.0, "references": ["https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/8f01f886cc5e7bbc16cbf1a9928fdebbc911e973", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/2be39946abcde5a6416fb074ef728429e246a996", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/522d6dcdc645d8f97d6b4cdfd6d8eea307f3ff0e", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/9a756f277eb89f769dbf380f38245c270d31fdb5", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/32d6df14fdab71fe1ba304fd9a0db0411ea2e043", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/97ca58b0fb026799b99e3d552d5f69cf9a3113ad", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/47049fdadc0eaa115e813735b827e1379c0d2cf8", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/0918ee2c0eeb4d7f45b82b3dc11e65c2d9b7ad59"], "aliases": ["GHSA-vhpc-fmr8-vgcc", "CVE-2026-89864"], "assigner": "Linux", "epss": 0.21, "enisaIdProduct": [{"id": "03479a42-c9df-3b08-ba92-a94172d3faf1", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "9ebb5d9c69f1f5721f9f6f49e501c674c1e184ae <97ca58b0fb026799b99e3d552d5f69cf9a3113ad"}, {"id": "054eb2f8-33de-309d-b891-786a6686621b", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "9ebb5d9c69f1f5721f9f6f49e501c674c1e184ae <2be39946abcde5a6416fb074ef728429e246a996"}, {"id": "56f20e21-785d-3ee0-9c2c-be12a000b176", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 7.2.5"}, {"id": "62f911f7-ce9f-3905-93fa-84150186230b", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "9ebb5d9c69f1f5721f9f6f49e501c674c1e184ae <47049fdadc0eaa115e813735b827e1379c0d2cf8"}, {"id": "762b8704-af4b-3365-b15a-dffbd357e9ea", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 7.3"}, {"id": "7b04d2c5-dbad-3d5e-8a9a-7a6f1ddd51f9", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "9ebb5d9c69f1f5721f9f6f49e501c674c1e184ae <522d6dcdc645d8f97d6b4cdfd6d8eea307f3ff0e"}, {"id": "7fe03cdd-07f0-38c4-ad73-23a07148b058", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 6.1.188"}, {"id": "8cabe6a2-be9c-3fda-a301-9ec01057fc3e", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "3.7"}, {"id": "9f32f747-36d8-3032-b1dc-7fddb99120bb", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 6.6.157"}, {"id": "aa54cfbc-f171-3978-ace5-dd3ad80dfba7", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 6.18.51"}, {"id": "be312100-2d3b-356e-8003-b0a142af4069", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 6.12.110"}, {"id": "c47d6b7d-999c-3ac8-8360-3497c846c80c", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "